            "notes": "By the sixth round, you should purchase [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98) but if you did really good you should also have enough points to get [Resurrection Rangefinder](item_99baffec-51b5-42e4-be61-e29f3de8219f)\n\nBoth will give you massive survivability boosts, ensuring a clean and high-performing round from every angle.\n\nWith [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98), you\u2019ll have a constant healing source that, combined with your flight speed, will drive your enemies crazy.\n\nWith [Resurrection Rangefinder](item_99baffec-51b5-42e4-be61-e29f3de8219f), you\u2019ll be able to res your teammates from a greater distance \u2014 which, by this point, becomes absolutely essential.\n\nJust remember: as the game progresses, not only you, but also your enemies will have more tools in their arsenal!\nEven if you\u2019ve got plenty of survival options, that doesn\u2019t make you invisible \u2014 use your brain!\n\nHere on the side, I\u2019m using the cheaper version, because after testing the build, I realized that \u2014 unless you're with a solid team \u2014 you might sometimes struggle to earn extra points.\n\nThis is just to show you that even if a few rounds don\u2019t go as planned, it doesn\u2019t mean the build is inefficient \u2014 quite the opposite!\nI\u2019ve been through many different situations, and sometimes I even ended up using blue powers when I should\u2019ve had purples.\nYou just need to compensate for whatever issues you\u2019re facing, and everything will go smoothly.\nThe beauty of Stadium is that you can adapt \u2014 even when you\u2019re being hard-countered \ud83d\ude01",
